<title>CHINA: China '97 sugar crop seen at 88 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>China '97 sugar crop seen at 88 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's sugar crop is expected to reach 88 million tonnes in 1997, the Futures Herald newspaper said on Thursday quoting a forecast by the Ministry of Internal Trade.</p>
<p>China's sugar crop in 1996 reached a total of 82.5 million tonnes, including 67 million tonnes of sugar cane and 15.5 million tonnes of sugar beet, official figures showed.</p>
<p>The projected increase this year largely reflected a rise in acreage under sugar crops, the newspaper said, without giving further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
